/*  EXPECTED: COMPILES and runs; compiled output must match the interpreter.

    A function copies a tree: it writes a node out and inserts the copies of its children into that
    node's own field. Cast inside a rabbit on a tree from outside it.

    A field of an object written out in a body is a series of its own, not something the object
    might hold, so the copies go into the new node and not into the tree it was given (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O2). */

Define object tree-node with (the number label, the series of tree-node children).
Bind tree-node to copied, given (the tree-node original):
    Define copy as a new tree-node { the label original's label, the children a series of tree-node }.
    For each child in original's children, repeat:
        Insert cast copied on (child) into copy's children.
    Done.
    Return copy.
Done.
Define root as a new tree-node { the label 1, the children a series of tree-node }.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define twin as cast copied on (root).
    State twin's label.
Done.

/*  Make and drop enough values that freed memory is handed out again. */
Define churn as a series of text.
Define tick as 0.
While tick is less than 400, repeat:
    Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
    tick becomes tick + 1.
Done.
